"q-337996" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "homogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x{y}^{′}-y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x}$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y+x=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x{y}^{′}-y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y+x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y=-x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-x,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "150eef360fa6ca4370556dd37534d366c488edc736bb946f58aa913b35ef5b0b"} {"question" "q-337990" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-337990" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"