=4x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-338006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "150eef360fa6ca4370556dd37534d366c488edc736bb946f58aa913b35ef5b0b"} {"question" "q-338006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-338006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-338006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "homogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/state.json" "file_sha256" "9fa1041c8920fa9ae00c2a70d0ddbeafb4ca245ae19850ea3678670e61672839"} {"question" "q-338006" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer